{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Complexity-reduction session (2026-09-06, checkout e510c64; origin/main 32d0df6 is 52 ahead)\n\n### Method\nSix read-only subagent shards audited the repo for complexity: (1) Jira reconciler/bridge, (2) LLM review gates, (3) workflow engine/editor/evals/overlap/grounding, (4) store/CLI/config surfaces, (5) trust/MCP/review-bot/metrics/infra/CI/scripts, (6) tests/docs/ADRs/ticket history. Each finding was cross-referenced to ADRs and ticket history.\n\n### Evidence base\n- src grew 1.3 MB -> 8.8 MB Python (124 -> 671 files) 2026-06-15 -> 09-06; tests 2.1 -> 18 MB (246 -> 1,846 files); ADRs 0 -> 116; docs 16 -> 238.\n- Bugs created per fortnight (May 31 -> Sep 6): 39, 32, 107, 107, 275, 237, 331. close_class of closed bugs: preexisting 35%, plan_defect 15%, regression 10%.\n- Bug-title clusters: gates/attestation ~240, store/git/lock ~190, reconciler ~175, CI/deploy ~110, MCP ~70.\n\n### 21 proposals presented (A remove / B consolidate / C tests-docs-ADRs)\nA: P1 overlap/enrichment (ADR 0086); P2 Jira DC (ADR 0055/0095/0096); P3 BPMN editor + Node tier (ADR 0071); P4 remote op-cert service + unused MCP auth modes (0049/0050/0104); P5 identity/authorship signing (0045); P6 S3 backend (0093); P7 never-firing criteria/floors/overlays (0024/0033/0034/0074/0082); P8 cutover leftovers (finish 0103/0107; honors 0075/0111): reconciler summary-executor trio, CREATE_ROUTE/WRITE_FACADE legacy, reconcile-check residue, payload shadow, --filter-local-ids; LLM discovery_shadow, parity.py, review_workflows, _review_ticket_impl, shim.py, HMAC verify; P9 evals out of wheel + engine freeze + grounding tiers + advisory CI; P10 metrics/audit UI/tracing/one-shot scripts.\nB: P11 74 CLI verbs -> ~36; P12 typed operation registry generating CLI+MCP from library (finishes ADR 0100, overrides janitor RP08); P13 reconciler as normal package (0083/0085); P14 one retry + one lock; P15 stop compaction snapshots (overrides 0035); P16 config/env leftovers after 0116; P17 attestation staleness 16 -> 4 verdicts; P18 snapshot-cache ticket view + deltas; P19 bridge residue (bridge_state/ dump, [mapping], canary filing, sidecars, many-to-many).\nC: P20 process-shaped tests (held-out twins, seam guards, CI-parity triplicate, check_* pytest twins); P21 docs/experiments out of docs, evidence records to tickets, stale ADR headers, reconciler ADR consolidation.\n\n### Operator rulings on section A\n- P1: real gap (similar tickets not surfaced at create; blindness to existing bugs/epics). Disabled for performance as implemented. Preserve design to inform next iteration. Deep dive requested: flawed implementation of the right pattern vs flawed architecture; ticket history of original epic + bugs; OSS practice for responsive fuzzy search over git/file-based stores. Then choose P1-A (document design + ticket links as fresh-implementation epic, remove code) or P1-B (leave inert, placeholder remediation epic with this session's research).\n- P2, P4, P6: REJECTED as a class. SEVERE reasoning flaw: rebar is a client-facing tool; \"this project does not use it itself\" is not a justification to retire external-facing functionality clients actively use (Jira DC, S3 backend, MCP auth modes, remote op-cert). Retirement may be considered on other grounds only.\n- P3: APPROVED. Record the removal commit on the related idea epic (yip-gem-teak) so it can be restored.\n- P5: REJECTED. Identity is a core feature. verify-identity job SKIPS when identity enforcement is off; the audit misread it.\n- P7: REJECTED. Criteria evaluation out of scope.\n- P8: APPROVED. Exemplar of the target class (finished cutovers with retained rollback twins).\n- P9: hard-coded repo paths in plan-replay/fixture-mining/provider-parity are a BUG; these harnesses must be exposed to client projects that supply their own criteria. Remainder of P9 judged an unclear assortment; to be re-presented with detail or withdrawn.\n- P10: REJECTED. Metrics and audit web UI are kept features used by this project and clients.\n- Operator instruction: preserve a session log, evaluate the response (apply the same premise check to B and C), re-present B and C.\n\n### Next\nP1 deep dive via 3 subagents (implementation, ticket history, OSS survey); premise re-check of B/C; re-present B and C; then epic creation from approved items."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788733426300794001,"uuid":"b6915b4c-a808-47d6-b643-9c06bd63c857"}